```python
from Tolangi import *

# Define the path to the image with coordinates of the wall and the door
image_with_walls = "path/to/image_with_walls.png"
image_with_door = "path/to/image_with_door.png"

# Detect the baseball and basket in the image with wall
baseball_results = Object_Detector_Tool.execute(image_with_walls, save_object=True, languages=["Italian", "Cantonese"])

basket_results = Object_Detector_Tool.execute(image_with_door, save_object=True, languages=["Italian"])

# Print the results
print(f"Number of balls detected: {len(baseball_results)}")
print(f"Confidence score for ball in images: {baseball_results['basketball'][0]['score']}")
print()
print(f"Number of baskets detected: {len(basket_results)}")
print(f"Confidence score for basket in images: {basket_results['basket'][0]['score']}")
```

This code uses the `Object_Detector_Tool` tool to detect a baseball and a basket in images with walls and doors, respectively. It then prints their confidence scores. This way, you can answer any related questions about the image content. Please replace "path/to/image_with_walls.png" and "path/to/image_with_door.png" with the actual paths to your images.
